// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/turbobaby/client_errors.t27 -- what a customer is told when something fails, and what
; the browser is allowed to report back.
; Two halves of one boundary. Outward: a failed request must reach the customer as a sentence he
; can act on, never as a numeral and never as nothing. Inward: an unauthenticated browser may
; post a failure report, and the bounds on that post are the only thing between a diagnostic and
; an open write endpoint. This file owns the rules on both sides. It owns no message text, no
; catalog vocabulary, no money and no identity: whether a request PROVED who it is belongs to
; request_identity.t27, what an unpublished locale resolves to belongs to locale_policy.t27, the
; read API's wire numerals belong to catalog_api.t27, and the discipline that an absence is not a
; number belongs to pricing_honesty.t27, and the sliding-window limiter itself belongs to
; rate_limit.t27. All six edges (seven since 2026-09-22) are named below by ID; none is restated.
; --
; WHY (measured 2026-09-21). The intake at src/api/client_errors.rs:56 takes a POST from anyone:
; the module says so at :8-9, and check_admin appears exactly twice in the whole 847-line file,
; at :117 and :519, both on GET handlers. Neither POST is gated. Five independent bounds hold that
; open door, they are listed below in the order they act, and only the first of them runs before
; the body is deserialized. FOUR of the five live in this file and only the body limit lives
; elsewhere (src/api/mod.rs:105). Of those four, two are named constants -- the rate at :39-41 and
; the caps at :49-52 -- and two are written into the handler's own arms: shape at :178-185,
; :304-306 and :633-645, sanitizing at :196-232. Not one of the four sits in a shared module, which
; is why a contract for the limiter does not amount to a contract for this endpoint: the mechanism
; is general and the budget is local. (An earlier draft of this header said THREE and named only
; the two constant blocks; the count and the lines it cited disagreed, and the lines were right.)
; --
; WHY THE ALERT SIDE NEEDED A CONTRACT TOO (measured 2026-09-21). should_alert (:359-379) has two
; triggers and one of them cannot fire. The fatal branch at :365 requires source == window.onerror
; -- but the only production call site (:430-434) passes err.source, and err.source came out of
; normalize_source (:297, :178-185), which returns wasm, android, ios or unknown and nothing else.
; The shipped Mini App is the single sender to this endpoint (src/ui/components/error_overlay.rs:155)
; and it sends exactly three source values, at :192, :245 and :303; not one of them survives
; normalization, so every report the shop actually receives is stored as unknown. The consequence
; is measurable: the only live trigger is the purchase-path test at :376, so a panic anywhere but
; /cart or /checkout pages nobody. Three unit tests (:787, :794, :803) call should_alert with the
; raw source directly and pass, which is why the dead branch reads as covered.
; --
; WHERE THE BRIEF IS REFUTED. Five corrections, each measured.
;   1. "The four routes" (:56-59) is the right count and the right lines, but they are not four
;      error routes: :58 is GET /admin/promo-report, a sales report, and the module says at
;      :510-513 why it lodges here. Three of the four are telemetry; two are writes.
;   2. The error panel IS position:fixed across the top half at z-index 99999 and IS
;      tap-swallowing while open -- error_overlay.rs:55 and :58 -- but that is no longer the
;      default state. :30 starts it collapsed and :36-50 renders a badge instead; the panel opens
;      only on the customer's own tap at :46. The survey describes the shape before the repair
;      the same file's comment at :25-29 explains. Both facts are pinned below, because the
;      geometry is still one tap away.
;   3. "Every failure has a localized message and no failure renders a bare code" holds on one of
;      the two mappers and is refuted on the other, at exactly one line. api_errors.rs:35-48 sends
;      every status to a key, unknown included (:45). checkout_errors.rs:33 returns a formatted
;      numeral in one hardcoded language, bypassing the lookup, and it is reachable from
;      src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:1112. Two of its own tests pin it there (:155-160 asserts
;      the numeral is present, :197-204 asserts both locales get the identical string).
;   4. api_errors.rs:18-19 calls the checkout mapper "a thin wrapper" for the general one. It is
;      not one: checkout_errors.rs holds an independent match and a grep of that file for
;      api_errors returns zero. The two tables agree on seven arms and diverge on the eighth.
;   5. The brief named four reuse edges for this file. Two more were owed and could not have been
;      listed, because neither contract existed when it was written: a grep of specs/ on
;      2026-09-21 finds turbobaby/rate-limit, which owns the limiter this endpoint configures and
;      already records the shared-store tripwire this file would otherwise have declared a second
;      time, and turbobaby/observability, which owns metric names. Both are taken as edges below.
;      RE-VERIFIED 2026-09-21 over the 43 files the corpus now holds -- 42 under specs/turbobaby
;      plus specs/agents/turbobaby.t27 -- where both contracts are manifested and both still own
;      what is named here. The count of edges is six and has not moved since.
; --
; WHAT THIS FILE NEVER DOES. It quotes no message: every customer-facing sentence on this surface
; is a Russian or English row in src/trios/i18n.rs, pinned here by the line that selects it and
; never by its wording (L3, and the precedent pricing_honesty.t27 set). It carries no stack trace,
; no fixture of one, and no sample report. It names no customer: the intake accepts a
; client-supplied telegram_id and derives none from headers (:10-11), and no value of that field,
; real or invented, appears here. It declares no retention period, because the code implements
; none, and the honest refusal is recorded rather than a plausible number. It re-declares no HTTP
; numeral the corpus already has: the one numeral below is 202, and RE-MEASURED 2026-09-21 over
; all 43 files a grep for a declaration of it returns this file's line and no other, so no sibling
; owns it. The three refusals name their existing declaration sites instead. Nothing from D14 --
; no renter, handle, phone, key code, plate, debt, purchase price or personal note -- in a
; constant, a comment or a test.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module turbobaby-client-errors;

pub const KIND : str = "failure-contract";
pub const ID : str = "turbobaby/client-errors";
pub const NAME : str = "TurboBaby client failure reporting and message rules";
pub const WORLD : str = "gHashTag/turbobaby-user-bot";
pub const MEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-21";

; --- Sources ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pub const INTAKE_SOURCE : str = "src/api/client_errors.rs";
pub const RATE_SOURCE : str = "src/api/rate_limit.rs";
pub const FILTER_SOURCE : str = "src/trios/js_errors.rs";
pub const OVERLAY_SOURCE : str = "src/ui/components/error_overlay.rs";
pub const MESSAGE_SOURCES : [2]str = ["src/trios/api_errors.rs", "src/trios/checkout_errors.rs"];
pub const INTAKE_WITNESS : str = "tests/integration_client_errors.rs";
; wc -l over the tracked source, 2026-09-21. Recorded so "the whole file" is a measurement.
pub const INTAKE_SOURCE_LINES : u16 = 847;
pub const FILTER_SOURCE_LINES : u16 = 125;
pub const OVERLAY_SOURCE_LINES : u16 = 337;

; --- Ownership edges ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The pinned compiler lowers a brace import to an empty UseDecl and the gate rejects it, so a
; cross-contract edge is a string naming the owner's ID plus a test asserting the literal.
; catalog-api owns the wire numerals of the READ API and this file declines to declare a second
; copy of any of them. locale-policy owns what happens to a key with no translation, so this file
; takes key_has_translation as a boolean and states no fallback of its own. request-identity owns
; who a request is, which is why intake_outcome below has no identity argument at all: the write
; surface never consults an id, so it has nothing to leak about one. pricing-honesty owns the
; discipline that an absent number is not a number, applied here as the refusal to let any failure
; render an amount.
; The fifth and sixth edges were not in this file's brief, because neither contract existed when
; the brief was written; both were measured in the corpus on 2026-09-21 and both are load-bearing.
; rate-limit owns the sliding-window mechanism, the key-source order, the shared fallback bucket
; and -- in full, with the missing key prefix named -- the tripwire that these two POSTs draw on
; one store. None of that is restated here: this file declares only the BUDGET the intake binds
; that mechanism to, and takes the limiter's verdict as the boolean under_rate_limit.
; observability owns metric names and what a metric may say, so the count below of accepted event
; names that reach no metric is stated as a gap in this endpoint's allow-list and never as a
; claim about the metric vocabulary.
pub const REUSES_CATALOG_API_ID : str = "turbobaby/catalog-api";
pub const REUSES_LOCALE_POLICY_ID : str = "turbobaby/locale-policy";
pub const REUSES_REQUEST_IDENTITY_ID : str = "turbobaby/request-identity";
pub const REUSES_PRICING_HONESTY_ID : str = "turbobaby/pricing-honesty";
pub const REUSES_RATE_LIMIT_ID : str = "turbobaby/rate-limit";
pub const REUSES_OBSERVABILITY_ID : str = "turbobaby/observability";
; The seventh edge, added 2026-09-22 with the order cancellation's surface (see "What a customer is
; told"). order-presentation owns what the order screens DO around the answer -- when the dialog
; closes, when the status is read again, when Confirm may send, and what the screen did before
; that day -- and this file owns only which sentence each answer gets. Its record of the screen is
; consumed by declaration name and not restated.
pub const REUSES_ORDER_PRESENTATION_ID : str = "turbobaby/order-presentation";
pub const REUSE_EDGE_COUNT : u8 = 7;
pub const REUSE_EDGE_COUNT_BEFORE_THE_CANCEL_SURFACE : u8 = 6;
pub const CANCEL_SCREEN_RECORD_DECLARATION : str = "CANCEL_ANSWER_WAS_TOLD_BEFORE_REPAIR and CANCEL_DIALOG_CLOSED_ON_EVERY_ANSWER_BEFORE_REPAIR, declared by the order-presentation contract";
pub const NO_TRANSLATION_OUTCOME_INPUT : str = "key_has_translation, supplied by the locale contract";
pub const LIMITER_VERDICT_INPUT : str = "under_rate_limit, supplied by the rate-limit contract";
pub const SHARED_BUCKET_TRIPWIRE_IS_RESTATED_HERE : bool = false;
pub const KEY_SOURCE_RULE_IS_RESTATED_HERE : bool = false;
pub const WHO_A_REQUEST_IS_IS_NOT_THIS_FILES_SUBJECT : bool = true;
pub const FAILURE_CARRIES_A_PRICE : bool = false;

; --- The intake surface ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; routes() at src/api/client_errors.rs:54-60 registers four paths. Two are POST writes (:56, :59)
; and two are admin-gated GET reads (:57, :58). Only three are about client telemetry; :58 is a
; promo sales report lodged here for the reason the module gives at :510-513, and this file judges
; nothing about it beyond counting it.
pub const ROUTE_COUNT : u8 = 4;
pub const WRITE_ROUTE_COUNT : u8 = 2;
pub const ADMIN_READ_ROUTE_COUNT : u8 = 2;
pub const TELEMETRY_ROUTE_COUNT : u8 = 3;
pub const UNRELATED_ROUTE_COUNT : u8 = 1;
; check_admin occurs exactly twice in the file, at :117 and :519, both on the GET handlers.
; Neither POST calls it or any other gate, and the module states the reason at :8-9: a failure
; that happens before login must still be reportable.
pub const INTAKE_GATE_COUNT : u8 = 0;
pub const INTAKE_IS_UNAUTHENTICATED_BY_DESIGN : bool = true;

pub fn route_is_gated(route_is_admin_read: bool) bool {
  return route_is_admin_read;
}

; --- What stops this from being an open write endpoint --------------------------------------------
; Five bounds, listed in the order they act. Only the first runs before the body is deserialized.
pub const BOUND_COUNT : u8 = 5;
; 1. Body size. src/api/mod.rs:105 layers DefaultBodyLimit::max(2 * 1024 * 1024) over the merged
; router that took client_errors::routes() at :94. The numeral the framework answers with is not
; measured in this repository, so this file pins the byte bound and declines the status.
pub const BODY_LIMIT_BYTES : u32 = 2097152;
pub const BODY_LIMIT_ACTS_BEFORE_DESERIALIZATION : bool = true;
pub const BODY_LIMIT_REFUSAL_STATUS_IS_MEASURED : bool = false;
; 2. Rate. The three numbers at :39-41 are this endpoint's budget and live nowhere else: the
; limiter takes window, ceiling and key cap as arguments, so a contract for the limiter fixes none
; of them. What differs from the admin gate -- turbobaby/request-identity records that gate in
; ADMIN_RL_WINDOW_SECONDS, ADMIN_RL_MAX_ATTEMPTS, ADMIN_RL_MAX_TRACKED_IPS and
; ADMIN_RL_COUNTS_FAILURES_ONLY, named by declaration rather than by line because a sibling's
; lines move on its next edit -- is the window and the counting rule: 60 seconds against 300, and
; every request counted here against
; failures only there. The tracked-key cap is 10000 on both, which is a coincidence of two
; separate literals (src/api/client_errors.rs:41 and src/api/auth.rs:433-435) and not a shared
; constant; neither file would change if the other did. Who ends up in which bucket, and what
; happens when two handlers draw on one store, belong to the limiter contract named above.
pub const RATE_WINDOW_SECONDS : u16 = 60;
pub const RATE_MAX_REQUESTS : u8 = 10;
pub const RATE_MAX_TRACKED_KEYS : u32 = 10000;
pub const RATE_COUNTS_EVERY_REQUEST : bool = true;
pub const RATE_BUDGET_IS_DECLARED_AT_THE_CALL_SITE : bool = true;
pub const KEY_CAP_COINCIDES_WITH_THE_ADMIN_GATE : bool = true;
pub const WINDOW_COINCIDES_WITH_THE_ADMIN_GATE : bool = false;
; 3. Shape. A message that is empty after trimming is refused at :304-306. The source field is
; normalized to a closed four-value set at :178-185, and the event name to a closed allow-list at
; :633-645, so a hostile client cannot mint a label or a time-series name.
pub const SOURCE_VALUE_COUNT : u8 = 4;
pub const MESSAGE_IS_REQUIRED : bool = true;
; 4. Truncation. :49-52, applied at :298-326 -- after deserialization, so it bounds the row and
; not the request.
pub const SERVER_MESSAGE_CAP_CHARS : u16 = 2000;
pub const SERVER_STACK_CAP_CHARS : u16 = 1000;
pub const SERVER_URL_PATH_CAP_CHARS : u16 = 500;
pub const SERVER_USER_AGENT_CAP_CHARS : u16 = 500;
; 5. Sanitizing. :196-232 strips initData-shaped tokens from every free-text field before storage,
; which the module calls defense in depth at :193-195.
pub const SANITIZER_PRECEDES_TRUNCATION : bool = true;
pub const SANITIZER_RUNS_ON_EVERY_FREE_TEXT_FIELD : bool = true;

; The limiter's admission rule is the limiter contract's, parameterized by a ceiling. This binds
; it to the ceiling this endpoint passes, which is the only part of it that lives here. The
; boundary matters both ways: the ceiling is the first REFUSED count and not the last admitted
; one, and that off-by-one is a property of the rule rather than of the number.
pub fn budget_admits(prior_requests_in_window: u8) bool {
  return prior_requests_in_window < RATE_MAX_REQUESTS;
}

; --- Outcomes -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Discriminants rather than numerals, because three of the four numerals are already declared in
; this corpus for other surfaces and a second copy would be the duplication the owner forbids.
; OUTCOME_COUNT is the exclusive bound of the discriminant range, so it counts the unset slot as
; well: four outcomes and one UNSET. SURFACE_COUNT and RENDER_KIND_COUNT further down count only
; their real members, because no predicate ranges over either.
pub const OUTCOME_UNSET : u8 = 0;
pub const OUTCOME_ACCEPTED : u8 = 1;
pub const OUTCOME_MALFORMED : u8 = 2;
pub const OUTCOME_THROTTLED : u8 = 3;
pub const OUTCOME_SINK_FAILED : u8 = 4;
pub const OUTCOME_COUNT : u8 = 5;
; The one numeral this file declares. RE-MEASURED 2026-09-21 over all 43 files of the corpus: a
; grep for a declaration of 202 in specs/ returns this file's line and no other. It appears in
; neither turbobaby/catalog-api's set, which owns HTTP_BAD_REQUEST and HTTP_INTERNAL_ERROR, nor
; turbobaby/request-identity's, which owns HTTP_TOO_MANY_REQUESTS -- both named by ID and
; DECLARATION rather than by line, because a line in a sibling goes stale on that sibling's next
; edit. It is the fact that distinguishes this surface: the handler returns
; it at :477 after the row is written but while the admin alert is still an unawaited task spawned
; at :462, so the answer acknowledges the report without waiting on anything it causes. The
; integration witness pins it at tests/integration_client_errors.rs:45 and :125.
pub const HTTP_ACCEPTED : u16 = 202;
pub const CORPUS_FILES_AT_REMEASUREMENT : u8 = 43;
pub const SIBLINGS_DECLARING_THIS_NUMERAL : u8 = 0;
pub const HTTP_STATUS_OWNED_ELSEWHERE : u16 = 0;
pub const MALFORMED_NUMERAL_ALREADY_DECLARED_AT : str = "turbobaby/catalog-api";
pub const SINK_FAILED_NUMERAL_ALREADY_DECLARED_AT : str = "turbobaby/catalog-api";
pub const THROTTLED_NUMERAL_ALREADY_DECLARED_AT : str = "turbobaby/request-identity";

; Precedence mirrors the handler: the rate check at :387 runs before sanitize_request at :400,
; which runs before the insert at :404, so a throttled request is never judged by any rule this
; HANDLER owns. It is not the first judgement the caller meets, and the difference is worth stating
; rather than implying: the Json extractor in the signature at :384 deserializes before :387, so a
; body that is not valid JSON is refused without the throttle ever seeing it. message_present below
; is the empty-message refusal at :304-306 and nothing else.
pub fn intake_outcome(under_rate_limit: bool, message_present: bool, sink_wrote: bool) u8 {
  if (!under_rate_limit) {
    return OUTCOME_THROTTLED;
  }
  if (!message_present) {
    return OUTCOME_MALFORMED;
  }
  if (!sink_wrote) {
    return OUTCOME_SINK_FAILED;
  }
  return OUTCOME_ACCEPTED;
}

; The event endpoint has no message requirement -- the module says so at :544-546 -- so it has one
; fewer way to fail and shares every other bound.
pub fn event_intake_outcome(under_rate_limit: bool, sink_wrote: bool) u8 {
  if (!under_rate_limit) {
    return OUTCOME_THROTTLED;
  }
  if (!sink_wrote) {
    return OUTCOME_SINK_FAILED;
  }
  return OUTCOME_ACCEPTED;
}

pub fn outcome_is_known(outcome: u8) bool {
  return outcome >= OUTCOME_ACCEPTED and outcome < OUTCOME_COUNT;
}

pub fn outcome_http_status(outcome: u8) u16 {
  if (outcome == OUTCOME_ACCEPTED) {
    return HTTP_ACCEPTED;
  }
  return HTTP_STATUS_OWNED_ELSEWHERE;
}

; --- What is stored, and what is not --------------------------------------------------------------
pub fn sanitized_length(raw_len: u16, cap: u16) u16 {
  if (raw_len > cap) {
    return cap;
  }
  return raw_len;
}

; The two ends of the wire disagree about the stack and agree about the message. The browser caps
; the message at error_overlay.rs:109 and the stack at :110 before it sends; the server caps the
; stack at :50 before it stores, so 4000 characters of a long trace are produced, transmitted and
; then dropped.
pub const BROWSER_MESSAGE_CAP_CHARS : u16 = 2000;
pub const BROWSER_STACK_CAP_CHARS : u16 = 5000;
pub const MESSAGE_CAPS_AGREE : bool = true;
pub const STACK_CAPS_AGREE : bool = false;
; The in-memory panel list, error_overlay.rs:108, oldest dropped at :136-138.
pub const PANEL_REPORT_CAP : u8 = 50;

pub fn stack_survives_the_round_trip(browser_stack_chars: u16) bool {
  return browser_stack_chars <= SERVER_STACK_CAP_CHARS;
}

; A report is attributable only because a client chose to say so. The endpoint never derives an id
; from headers (:10-11), and the one shipped sender does not send one: a grep for telegram_id over
; src/ui/components/error_overlay.rs returns 0, and the payload it builds at :143-153 has no such
; field. The column exists and is nullable (migrations/048_client_error_logs.sql:14, with the
; reason at :3-5). No value of it is named anywhere in this file.
pub const ID_IS_DERIVED_FROM_HEADERS : bool = false;
pub const SHIPPED_SENDER_SUPPLIES_AN_ID : bool = false;

pub fn stored_report_is_attributable(client_supplied_positive_id: bool) bool {
  if (ID_IS_DERIVED_FROM_HEADERS) {
    return true;
  }
  return client_supplied_positive_id;
}

; The event allow-list at :633-645 accepts eight names and the metric dispatch at :604-626 has
; seven arms. The odd one is checkout_retry_clicked (:637): stored under its own name and counted
; by nothing. A name off the list is stored under the catch-all at :643, which is the truthful
; label and matches no arm either. The gap is stated as a property of THIS allow-list, which is
; an intake bound; what a metric is called and what it may say belongs to the observability
; contract named above, and no metric name appears here.
pub const EVENT_NAMES_ACCEPTED : u8 = 8;
pub const EVENT_NAMES_WITH_A_METRIC : u8 = 7;
pub const EVENT_NAMES_STORED_BUT_UNCOUNTED : u8 = 1;

pub fn stored_event_name_is_the_clients(name_in_allow_list: bool) bool {
  return name_in_allow_list;
}

pub fn event_reaches_a_metric(name_in_allow_list: bool, name_has_metric_arm: bool) bool {
  return name_in_allow_list and name_has_metric_arm;
}

; No retention. The mechanism exists -- audit_sweep_sql at src/db/orders.rs:670 serves three
; tables (:681, :725, :759) -- and neither telemetry table is enrolled in it: a grep for
; client_error_logs and client_event_logs over src/db/orders.rs returns 0, and a case-insensitive
; grep for a DELETE over either table across the whole tree returns two lines, both test cleanup
; (tests/integration_promo_agent.rs:337 and :392). So rows stay until someone removes them by
; hand, and this file states a period the code does not implement nowhere at all.
pub const TELEMETRY_RETENTION_IS_IMPLEMENTED : bool = false;
pub const AUDIT_SWEEP_MECHANISM_EXISTS : bool = true;
pub const TABLES_ENROLLED_IN_THE_SWEEP : u8 = 3;
pub const TELEMETRY_TABLES_ENROLLED_IN_THE_SWEEP : u8 = 0;
pub const TELEMETRY_RETENTION_NOTE : str = "No period is declared here because none is implemented. The sweep builder at src/db/orders.rs:670 is used by three audit tables and by neither telemetry table; the only DELETE over client_error_logs or client_event_logs anywhere in the tree is test cleanup at tests/integration_promo_agent.rs:337 and :392. Closing this needs an enrolled sweep, after which the period becomes a measurement instead of a wish.";

; --- What the browser is allowed to report back ---------------------------------------------------
; src/trios/js_errors.rs:48-50 is the rule, and it is a conjunction of two independent refusals,
; not a list. A message matching one of five noise spellings (:23-27) is refused whatever its
; location, because those are cancellations the browser performs on purpose. An opaque report is
; refused only when the browser described nothing at all: :40-45 requires the message to be one of
; three ways of saying nothing AND the filename empty AND the line zero AND the column zero. The
; narrowness is the point (:37-39) -- one present coordinate defeats it, so a real fault that
; merely lacks a line number still gets through. This file pins the shape and the counts; the
; spellings stay in the source.
pub const NOISE_SPELLING_COUNT : u8 = 5;
pub const ABSENT_MESSAGE_SPELLING_COUNT : u8 = 3;
pub const OPAQUE_REQUIRES_ALL_FOUR_ABSENCES : bool = true;

pub fn report_is_opaque(message_absent: bool, filename_absent: bool, line_absent: bool, column_absent: bool) bool {
  return message_absent and filename_absent and line_absent and column_absent;
}

pub fn listener_report_is_reportable(message_is_noise: bool, message_absent: bool, filename_absent: bool, line_absent: bool, column_absent: bool) bool {
  if (message_is_noise) {
    return false;
  }
  return !report_is_opaque(message_absent, filename_absent, line_absent, column_absent);
}

; --- Three intake paths, three different filters --------------------------------------------------
; Measured by grep over src/ui/components/error_overlay.rs: push_error has two callers (:248 and
; :306) and send_error_telemetry has three (:185, :247 and :305). So the browser has three ways to
; report and no two of them are treated alike. The listener registered at :266-267 applies the full
; rule at :238. The rejection handler applies only the noise half at :296, so an opaque promise
; rejection -- one whose reason could not be read, defaulted at :295 -- is reportable where the
; same emptiness on the listener path is not. report_panic (:184-193), called from src/lib.rs:40,
; applies nothing and reaches the server only: it never calls push_error, so a Rust panic is
; recorded and never shown.
pub const PATH_UNSET : u8 = 0;
pub const PATH_LISTENER : u8 = 1;
pub const PATH_REJECTION : u8 = 2;
pub const PATH_PANIC : u8 = 3;
pub const INTAKE_PATH_COUNT : u8 = 3;

pub fn path_is_known(path: u8) bool {
  return path >= PATH_LISTENER and path <= PATH_PANIC;
}

pub fn path_applies_the_opaque_filter(path: u8) bool {
  return path == PATH_LISTENER;
}

pub fn path_applies_the_noise_filter(path: u8) bool {
  return path == PATH_LISTENER or path == PATH_REJECTION;
}

pub fn path_reaches_the_panel(path: u8) bool {
  return path == PATH_LISTENER or path == PATH_REJECTION;
}

pub fn path_reaches_the_sink(path: u8) bool {
  return path_is_known(path);
}

; The consequence worth naming. On the two filtered paths the filter runs BEFORE both the panel
; and the sink (:238 before :247, :296 before :305), so there is no branch anywhere that records a
; report without showing it. Deciding a customer should not see something decides that nobody
; will. The panic path inverts it and is the only one that records without showing.
pub fn filtering_costs_the_record(path: u8) bool {
  return path_applies_the_noise_filter(path) and path_reaches_the_sink(path);
}

pub fn path_records_without_showing(path: u8) bool {
  return path_reaches_the_sink(path) and !path_reaches_the_panel(path);
}

; --- The panel as a customer-visible failure mode ---------------------------------------------------
; Verified against the source rather than taken from the survey. The expanded panel at
; error_overlay.rs:52-105 is position:fixed with top, left and right pinned to the edges (:55), is
; capped at half the viewport height (:58) and sits at z-index 99999 (:55): while it is open it is
; over the controls beneath it, which the file's own comment at :25-29 says cost the shop its
; checkout button twice. What the survey missed is the repair. :30 initializes the expanded signal
; to false, :36-50 renders a badge of 4-by-10 pixel padding in the corner instead, and the panel
; appears only when the customer taps it at :46. Nothing renders at all while the list is empty
; (:32-34), and an open panel has two ways out, collapse at :70 and clear at :79-82.
pub const PANEL_IS_FIXED : bool = true;
pub const PANEL_MAX_HEIGHT_VH : u8 = 50;
pub const PANEL_Z_INDEX : u32 = 99999;
pub const PANEL_IS_EXPANDED_BY_DEFAULT : bool = false;
pub const PANEL_OPENS_ONLY_ON_A_CUSTOMER_TAP : bool = true;
pub const PANEL_DISMISSAL_ROUTE_COUNT : u8 = 2;
pub const SURVEY_CALLED_THE_PANEL_THE_DEFAULT_STATE : bool = true;
pub const SURVEY_GEOMETRY_CLAIM_IS_CORRECT : bool = true;

pub fn anything_renders(any_report_held: bool) bool {
  return any_report_held;
}

pub fn panel_blocks_the_screen(any_report_held: bool, customer_expanded: bool) bool {
  return any_report_held and customer_expanded;
}

; --- The alert trigger that cannot fire ---------------------------------------------------------
; should_alert (:359-379) is a disjunction. The purchase-path half (:376) reads url_path, which
; survives sanitizing unchanged in shape, and fires. The fatal half (:365) reads source, which
; normalize_source has already collapsed to one of four values (:297 into :178-185), and the value
; it compares against is not one of them, so it is false at the one production call site whatever
; the message says. The cooldown at :43-47 is a single process-wide instant (:45-46), not a bucket
; per client, so one noisy hour of purchase-path failures suppresses every other page's alert too.
pub const ALERT_TRIGGER_COUNT : u8 = 2;
pub const ALERT_TRIGGERS_REACHABLE_IN_PRODUCTION : u8 = 1;
pub const SOURCE_IS_NORMALIZED_BEFORE_THE_ALERT_TEST : bool = true;
pub const ALERT_COOLDOWN_SECONDS : u16 = 300;
pub const ALERT_COOLDOWN_IS_GLOBAL : bool = true;
pub const ALERT_IS_SPAWNED_DETACHED : bool = true;

pub fn alert_fatal_branch_can_fire(source_is_normalized: bool) bool {
  return !source_is_normalized;
}

pub fn alert_is_raised(source_is_normalized: bool, message_is_fatal_shaped: bool, path_is_purchase: bool, within_cooldown: bool) bool {
  if (within_cooldown) {
    return false;
  }
  if (path_is_purchase) {
    return true;
  }
  return alert_fatal_branch_can_fire(source_is_normalized) and message_is_fatal_shaped;
}

; --- What a customer is told --------------------------------------------------------------------
; Two mappers, two surfaces, one divergence. api_errors.rs:35-48 has eight explicit arms and sends
; everything else to a key at :45, so no status escapes the table. checkout_errors.rs:25-34 has
; seven and sends everything else to a formatted numeral at :33. The eighth arm the general mapper
; has is 401, and api_errors.rs:11-14 gives the reason: checkout cannot see a stale session because
; it demands a fresh proof, but a long-lived screen can. The general mapper is live at ten call
; sites across six screens; the checkout mapper at src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:1112, which is
; where the bare-code branch is reachable from.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-22: three surfaces, not two. The census above counted the two status mappers
; and could not see a third place where a customer meets a failure: the order detail screen's own
; cancellation. Until that day it told the customer NOTHING about the answer -- a success, a refusal
; and a lost connection alike (CANCEL_SCREEN_RECORD_DECLARATION) -- which is the one render this
; file forbids (RENDER_EMPTY_STRING_IS_POSSIBLE), reached on a path neither mapper was on. Since then
; the answer is told by ORDER_CANCEL_READER, a function in src/trios/api_errors.rs, so
; MESSAGE_SOURCES still names the same two files. It DELEGATES to the general mapper where that
; mapper's sentence is true of a cancellation -- the expired session, the restricted account, the
; pace and the server, four status classes -- and chooses an existing key of its own everywhere
; else, because the general mapper's sentences for the other statuses speak of a cart, an item, a
; duplicate order and a price. Its choices are pinned by the tests in that file and are not restated
; here; ORDER_CANCEL_OWN_KEY_NAMES lists the keys it selects itself, by constant name. The server
; class is delegated late: a failure of the server's own leaves the outcome as unknown as no answer
; does, so it is told the two borrowed keys below while the status is read again, and the general
; mapper's server sentence only once that reading shows the order still pending
; (ORDER_CANCEL_SERVER_SENTENCE_WAITS_FOR_THE_CHECK). When the attempt may be repeated is the
; order-presentation contract's; which words it gets meanwhile is this file's.
; The two counts above stay exact and are now scoped: ten call sites across six screens counts the
; calls in src/ui/screens. The delegation is an eleventh call, in src/trios, and through it a seventh
; screen reaches the general mapper's sentences (API_MAPPER_DELEGATION_SITES counts every call
; outside the tests of the module that defines the mapper). No other trio module calls the mapper
; at all (TRIO_MODULES_CALLING_THE_API_MAPPER counts the modules that do, tests included).
; FAILURE_KEY_COUNT below stays the union of the keys the TWO status mappers select; the cancel
; surface's own keys are counted apart, and five of its six are outside that union.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-25, owner question D answered by delegation: "an existing key of its own
; everywhere else" no longer holds for one answer. The refusal the route makes itself -- 409, the
; order has left pending -- is told a key written for it, T_ORDER_DETAIL_CANCEL_REFUSED, and not
; this surface's fallback. The surface now selects seven keys of its own and six of them are
; outside that union; "five of its six" above is the count before that day
; (ORDER_CANCEL_OWN_KEY_COUNT_BEFORE_DELEGATION). What was decided, by whom and what it leaves
; open is CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_DECISION below.
pub const SURFACE_UNSET : u8 = 0;
pub const SURFACE_API : u8 = 1;
pub const SURFACE_CHECKOUT : u8 = 2;
pub const SURFACE_ORDER_CANCEL : u8 = 3;
pub const SURFACE_COUNT : u8 = 3;
pub const SURFACE_COUNT_BEFORE_THE_CANCEL_SURFACE : u8 = 2;
pub const ORDER_CANCEL_SURFACE_ADDED_AT : str = "2026-09-22";
pub const ORDER_CANCEL_READER : str = "order_cancel_line, src/trios/api_errors.rs";
pub const ORDER_CANCEL_READER_DELEGATES_TO_THE_API_MAPPER : bool = true;
pub const ORDER_CANCEL_DELEGATED_STATUS_CLASSES : u8 = 4;
pub const API_MAPPER_DELEGATION_SITES : u8 = 1;
pub const TRIO_MODULES_CALLING_THE_API_MAPPER : u8 = 1;
pub const API_MAPPER_REACHES_A_SCREEN_THROUGH_A_TRIO : bool = true;
pub const ORDER_CANCEL_SERVER_SENTENCE_WAITS_FOR_THE_CHECK : bool = true;
; The keys the cancel surface selects itself, answer by answer: the success, the missing order, the
; fallback it shares with the general mapper, the two it borrows from the success screen while an
; attempt whose outcome is unknown is checked, and the network key once the check has shown an
; unanswered attempt did not land. Gate 3 binds the set to the reader's arms, so a key the owner
; writes for question D has to arrive here as well. Only T_API_ERR_UNKNOWN is inside the union
; FAILURE_KEY_COUNT counts; the success key is not a failure key at all, and it had been written
; with the cancel feature and read by no screen until this surface existed.
; The key for question D arrived on 2026-09-25 as the seventh name, appended rather than inserted
; so that no index below moves. The fallback stays in the set: 400 -- the route's own answer to a
; malformed id or telegram_id -- and every other refusal that is not 401, 403, 404, 409 or 429
; still reaches it. The new key is selected by no status mapper, so it is outside the union too.
pub const ORDER_CANCEL_OWN_KEY_COUNT : u8 = 7;
pub const ORDER_CANCEL_OWN_KEY_COUNT_BEFORE_DELEGATION : u8 = 6;
pub const ORDER_CANCEL_OWN_KEY_NAMES : [7]str = [
  "T_ORDER_DETAIL_CANCELLED_BY_USER",
  "T_ORDER_DETAIL_NOT_FOUND",
  "T_API_ERR_UNKNOWN",
  "T_SUCCESS_STATUS_LOADING",
  "T_SUCCESS_STATUS_ERROR",
  "T_CHECKOUT_ERR_NETWORK",
  "T_ORDER_DETAIL_CANCEL_REFUSED",
];
pub const ORDER_CANCEL_KEYS_OUTSIDE_THE_FAILURE_UNION : u8 = 6;
pub const ORDER_CANCEL_SUCCESS_KEY_WAS_READ_BY_NOTHING_BEFORE_THE_SURFACE : bool = true;
; Never nothing, and the one answer told by something other than a line. An answer always gets a
; sentence, with one exception that is not an empty render: an attempt whose outcome is unknown --
; no answer, or a failure of the server's own -- after a fresh reading shows the order has left
; pending. What that attempt did is then unknown for good, and the card's status label -- a
; translated key, re-read -- is the one true sentence, so no line is added under it. Before an
; answer arrives there is nothing to tell.
pub const ORDER_CANCEL_SETTLED_UNKNOWN_IS_TOLD_BY_THE_STATUS_LABEL : bool = true;
; Named refusals of this surface. The owner's rule for the bot's service receipt and cash desk has
; three outcomes, done, not done and unknown, and an unknown outcome is checked BEFORE it is
; repeated (brain:knowledge_base:840-845 and brain:knowledge_base:870-873). The screen follows
; it; the WORDS do not exist for the Mini App. An attempt whose outcome is unknown is told with
; two keys borrowed from the success screen, one saying the status is being updated and one saying
; it could not be loaded, which are true of what the screen is doing and do not say, as the receipt
; does, that the outcome is unknown. And the refusal a cancellation meets once the order has left
; pending -- the order-presentation contract names it and its owner -- has no sentence at all: it
; is told this surface's fallback, T_API_ERR_UNKNOWN, whose invitation to try later is false for
; it. The nearest thing the owner has published is narrower than a principle: one precedent, in
; the bot's mileage-lowering flow, where a specific wording was struck because it tells the person
; nothing (brain:business_rules:1243-1245). The interim has that same fault, and it is recorded as
; a refusal of this file instead of being papered over. The missing-order line
; (T_ORDER_DETAIL_NOT_FOUND) carries no next step either, so the actionable-hint rule the general
; mapper's tests pin does not hold on this surface. Brain lines are the owner's knowledge
; base, a read-only dump read on 2026-09-22, translated and never transcribed, and no gate here
; checks them.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-25: the refusal is worded, and not by the owner. On that day the owner was put
; a numbered list of open questions and answered item 11 -- this question D -- by delegating it
; (translated: "I do not understand what this is; think it over"). A delegation approves no text;
; it hands the choice over. Under it the ru and en sentence was chosen the same day and ships as
; CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_KEY_NAME, which order_cancel_line selects for 409 alone and tells with the
; not-done tone. It is pinned here by the arm that selects it (ORDER_CANCEL_OWN_KEY_NAMES, which
; gate 3 binds) and never by its wording (L3); what it must do is CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_DECISION.
; The paragraph above stays as the record of 2026-09-22 to 2026-09-25, and so does the interim's
; name: T_API_ERR_UNKNOWN still answers the refusals that are not 409, and its fault is now theirs
; alone. Two limits of the chosen sentence are named rather than hidden. It describes the ORDER,
; where the note of 2026-09-22 asked for the ATTEMPT: it says the shop has the order in hand, which
; is true when the shop took it and false in the two other ways an order leaves pending before a
; customer's tap lands -- the shop rejected it, or an earlier attempt of the customer's own whose
; outcome was unknown did cancel it. In both, once the re-read that follows every answer lands, the
; card's status label beside the line reads cancelled, and the rest of the sentence stays true. And
; the next step it names is a person with no channel on the order card: nothing there links to the
; manager, and this change adds no link. Question D is closed by it. The unknown outcome's own
; sentence was never part of D and stays unwritten.
; REWORDED 2026-09-25, later the same day and under the same delegation, by the operator: the FIRST
; of the two limits above is CLOSED on that date. Dates here are UTC; the commit carries the
; working machine's +07:00 clock, which had already turned to the 26th. The paragraph above stays
; as the record of the first wording. The sentence no longer describes the order at all: it says
; that the app can no longer cancel this order, and it names the manager. Each clause of that is
; true whatever took the order out of pending -- the shop taking it, the shop rejecting it, or an
; earlier attempt of the customer's own whose outcome was unknown -- because cancel_order answers
; 409 (src/api/orders.rs, the status check before the update) for every stored
; status that is not pending, and the sentence says only what that answer means for the customer.
; So it is now true of every conflict (CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_SENTENCE_IS_TRUE_OF_EVERY_CONFLICT),
; which the first wording was not. Nothing else moved: the key keeps its name, the arm that selects
; it and every index above are unchanged, and the two rows in src/trios/i18n.rs were rewritten on
; their own lines, so no line citation into that file moved. The host tests in
; src/trios/api_errors.rs now also refuse any claim about what the shop is doing with the order. The
; SECOND limit stands: nothing on the order card links to the manager, and this change adds no link.
pub const CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_HAS_A_PUBLISHED_SENTENCE : bool = true;
pub const CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_HAD_A_PUBLISHED_SENTENCE_BEFORE_DELEGATION : bool = false;
pub const CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_KEY_NAME : str = "T_ORDER_DETAIL_CANCEL_REFUSED";
pub const CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_WORDED_AT : str = "2026-09-25";
pub const CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_WORDING_IS_THE_OWNERS_OWN : bool = false;
pub const CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_SENTENCE_IS_TRUE_OF_EVERY_CONFLICT : bool = true;
pub const CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_FIRST_WORDING_WAS_TRUE_OF_EVERY_CONFLICT : bool = false;
pub const CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_REWORDED_AT : str = "2026-09-25";
pub const CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_NAMED_LIMITS_OPEN : u8 = 1;
pub const CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_NAMED_LIMITS_OPEN_BEFORE_REWORDING : u8 = 2;
pub const CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_NEXT_STEP_HAS_A_CHANNEL_ON_THE_CARD : bool = false;
pub const CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_INTERIM_KEY_NAME : str = "T_API_ERR_UNKNOWN";
pub const CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_INTERIM_INVITES_A_REPEAT_THAT_CANNOT_SUCCEED : bool = true;
pub const UNKNOWN_CANCELLATION_HAS_A_PUBLISHED_SENTENCE : bool = false;
pub const ORDER_CANCEL_EVERY_REFUSAL_CARRIES_A_TRUE_NEXT_STEP : bool = false;
pub const OWNER_QUESTION_CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_SENTENCE_IS_OPEN : bool = false;
pub const CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_DECISION : str = "Owner question D, item 11 of the numbered list the owner answered on 2026-09-25. The answer, translated: I do not understand what this is; think it over. It delegates the wording and approves no text. Under it one ru and one en sentence were chosen the same day for the refusal cancel_order returns as 409 when the stored status is not pending, and they ship as T_ORDER_DETAIL_CANCEL_REFUSED in the two published locales (D13); the other six Lang variants read the English row, which is the locale-policy contract's fact. What the sentence must do, and the host tests in src/trios/api_errors.rs check: tell the customer the app will not cancel this order, not invite a repeat that meets the same refusal, name a next step -- the manager -- in both locales, and claim nothing about what the shop is doing with the order, since the same 409 answers an order the shop took, one it rejected and one already cancelled; the line is coloured not done and no other status is told it. The first wording, chosen earlier that day, said the order was already being handled, which is false for two of those three; the operator reworded it the same day, under the same delegation, to say only that the app can no longer cancel the order, which is true of every 409 (CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_REWORDED_AT). The owner may reword it at any time: that is a change of the two rows in src/trios/i18n.rs and of nothing in this file.";
pub const CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_NOTE : str = "Question D was answered on 2026-09-25 by delegation (CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_DECISION), and a 409 is told T_ORDER_DETAIL_CANCEL_REFUSED since. Of the two limits named that day, the first -- a sentence about the order whose first clause was false when the shop had rejected the order or an earlier attempt of the customer's own had cancelled it -- was closed the same day by rewording: the sentence now speaks only of what the app can no longer do, which holds for every 409. One thing remains, named: the manager the sentence points to has no channel on the order card. That is the owner's to change with the words, and it is not decided here.";
pub const CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_NOTE_BEFORE_REWORDING : str = "Question D was answered on 2026-09-25 by delegation (CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_DECISION), and a 409 is told T_ORDER_DETAIL_CANCEL_REFUSED since. Two things remain, both named: the sentence describes the order and not the attempt, so its first clause is false when the order left pending by the shop rejecting it or by an earlier attempt of the customer's own, whose outcome was unknown, landing -- the re-read status label beside it then reads cancelled; and the manager it names has no channel on the order card. Either is the owner's to change with the words, and neither is decided here.";
pub const CONFLICTED_CANCELLATION_NOTE_BEFORE_DELEGATION : str = "Owner question D. What is missing is an owner-approved ru and en sentence for a cancellation the server refused because the order had already left pending. No source publishes one: the owner's knowledge base has no node for the Mini App, DECISIONS.md fixes only the two locales (D13), and the bot's copy has a sentence for a cancelled order and none for a refused cancellation. What the knowledge base does publish is a principle for the bot, not copy: three outcomes and a check before a repeat, a refusal that names its object and explains (brain:knowledge_base:944-946 and brain:knowledge_base:953), and, narrower than a principle, one precedent from the bot's mileage-lowering flow: a specific wording struck because it tells the person nothing (brain:business_rules:1243-1245). The interim T_API_ERR_UNKNOWN has the fault that precedent names. The sentence must describe the ATTEMPT and not the order, because the same refusal answers a second attempt made after a first one whose outcome was unknown and that did cancel. Whether the sentence offers a next step, and which, is the owner's to choose with the words: one existing candidate is T_BIKE_ASK_MANAGER, which the bike card shows only when the Mini App can read the bot's username and which links to the bot's chat, and no channel is chosen here.";
pub const UNKNOWN_CANCELLATION_NOTE : str = "An attempt whose outcome is unknown -- no answer, or a failure of the server's own -- is told T_SUCCESS_STATUS_LOADING while the status is read again and T_SUCCESS_STATUS_ERROR when that read fails. Once a fresh reading shows the order still pending, trying again is a checked repeat, and the attempt is told T_CHECKOUT_ERR_NETWORK after no answer and the general mapper's server sentence after a failure of the server's own. All of these are true of what the screen does. None says in the owner's words that the outcome is unknown, because no such sentence is published for the Mini App; the bot's service receipt has one (brain:knowledge_base:843-845). A dedicated key needs a sentence of its own: question D, answered on 2026-09-25, wrote one for the refusal only.";
pub const API_MAPPED_ARM_COUNT : u8 = 8;
pub const CHECKOUT_MAPPED_ARM_COUNT : u8 = 7;
pub const EXTRA_ARM_IS_THE_EXPIRED_SESSION : bool = true;
pub const API_MAPPER_CALL_SITES : u8 = 10;
pub const API_MAPPER_CALL_SITE_SCREENS : u8 = 6;
; The union of the keys the two mappers can select, counted in src/trios/i18n.rs: the seven shared
; status keys at :253-259, the two body-code keys at :264-265, and the two the general mapper adds
; at :272-273. Eleven distinct keys; no wording of any of them is repeated here.
pub const FAILURE_KEY_COUNT : u16 = 11;
pub const CHECKOUT_MAPPER_IS_A_WRAPPER_OF_THE_API_MAPPER : bool = false;

pub fn surface_is_known(surface: u8) bool {
  return surface == SURFACE_API or surface == SURFACE_CHECKOUT or surface == SURFACE_ORDER_CANCEL;
}

; How a failure renders. Three outcomes and no fourth: the lookup answers with a translation, or
; with the key itself when the row is missing -- which is locale_policy.t27's fact and not restated
; here -- or the checkout surface skips the lookup entirely and formats the numeral. The empty
; string is not among them, which is the half of the brief's rule that survives measurement.
pub const RENDER_UNSET : u8 = 0;
pub const RENDER_LOCALIZED : u8 = 1;
pub const RENDER_BARE_KEY : u8 = 2;
pub const RENDER_BARE_CODE : u8 = 3;
pub const RENDER_KIND_COUNT : u8 = 3;
pub const RENDER_EMPTY_STRING_IS_POSSIBLE : bool = false;

pub fn render_kind(surface: u8, status_is_mapped: bool, key_has_translation: bool) u8 {
  if (surface == SURFACE_CHECKOUT and !status_is_mapped) {
    return RENDER_BARE_CODE;
  }
  if (!key_has_translation) {
    return RENDER_BARE_KEY;
  }
  return RENDER_LOCALIZED;
}

pub fn render_kind_is_known(kind: u8) bool {
  return kind >= RENDER_LOCALIZED and kind <= RENDER_BARE_CODE;
}

pub fn renders_a_bare_code(surface: u8, status_is_mapped: bool) bool {
  return render_kind(surface, status_is_mapped, true) == RENDER_BARE_CODE;
}

; Where the checkout sentence comes from. src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:1111-1112 tries the
; body code first and falls back to the status, so an unrecognized code (checkout_errors.rs:46
; returns nothing for one) never reaches the customer as a code -- it becomes the status sentence
; instead. Two codes were mapped, at :44 and :45; one is now, at :45.
; CHANGED 2026-09-25: the code at :44, "age_not_confirmed", lost its sentence when the owner
; removed the checkout's 20+ box for now (turbobaby/checkout-contact, AGE_BLOCKER_REMOVED_AT), and
; :44 is a comment line. The sentence was never reachable: the server's age refusal was a bare 422
; with no body. An unmapped code takes the status sentence, which is the path pinned below.
pub const MESSAGE_FROM_UNSET : u8 = 0;
pub const MESSAGE_FROM_BODY_CODE : u8 = 1;
pub const MESSAGE_FROM_STATUS : u8 = 2;
pub const MESSAGE_FROM_BARE_CODE : u8 = 3;
pub const MAPPED_BODY_CODE_COUNT : u8 = 1;
pub const MAPPED_BODY_CODE_COUNT_BEFORE_2026_09_25 : u8 = 2;
pub const UNKNOWN_BODY_CODE_IS_EVER_RENDERED : bool = false;

pub fn checkout_message_source(body_code_mapped: bool, status_is_mapped: bool) u8 {
  if (body_code_mapped) {
    return MESSAGE_FROM_BODY_CODE;
  }
  if (status_is_mapped) {
    return MESSAGE_FROM_STATUS;
  }
  return MESSAGE_FROM_BARE_CODE;
}

; --- Tests ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

test the_write_surface_carries_no_gate_and_the_read_surface_does {
  assert ROUTE_COUNT == 4;
  assert WRITE_ROUTE_COUNT + ADMIN_READ_ROUTE_COUNT == ROUTE_COUNT;
  assert TELEMETRY_ROUTE_COUNT + UNRELATED_ROUTE_COUNT == ROUTE_COUNT;
  assert INTAKE_GATE_COUNT == 0;
  assert route_is_gated(true) == true;
  assert route_is_gated(false) == false;
}

test the_budget_is_a_closed_count_per_window {
  assert budget_admits(0) == true;
  assert budget_admits(9) == true;
  assert budget_admits(RATE_MAX_REQUESTS) == false;
  assert budget_admits(255) == false;
  assert RATE_WINDOW_SECONDS == 60;
  assert RATE_BUDGET_IS_DECLARED_AT_THE_CALL_SITE == true;
}

test the_budget_differs_from_the_admin_gate_in_window_and_not_in_key_cap {
  assert WINDOW_COINCIDES_WITH_THE_ADMIN_GATE == false;
  assert KEY_CAP_COINCIDES_WITH_THE_ADMIN_GATE == true;
  assert RATE_MAX_TRACKED_KEYS == 10000;
  assert RATE_COUNTS_EVERY_REQUEST == true;
}

test the_limiter_mechanism_and_its_tripwire_are_not_restated_here {
  assert SHARED_BUCKET_TRIPWIRE_IS_RESTATED_HERE == false;
  assert KEY_SOURCE_RULE_IS_RESTATED_HERE == false;
  assert WHO_A_REQUEST_IS_IS_NOT_THIS_FILES_SUBJECT == true;
  assert REUSES_RATE_LIMIT_ID == "turbobaby/rate-limit";
  assert LIMITER_VERDICT_INPUT == "under_rate_limit, supplied by the rate-limit contract";
  assert NO_TRANSLATION_OUTCOME_INPUT == "key_has_translation, supplied by the locale contract";
}

test intake_precedence_refuses_before_it_inspects {
  assert intake_outcome(false, true, true) == OUTCOME_THROTTLED;
  assert intake_outcome(false, false, false) == OUTCOME_THROTTLED;
  assert intake_outcome(true, false, true) == OUTCOME_MALFORMED;
  assert intake_outcome(true, true, false) == OUTCOME_SINK_FAILED;
  assert intake_outcome(true, true, true) == OUTCOME_ACCEPTED;
}

test the_event_endpoint_has_one_fewer_way_to_fail {
  assert event_intake_outcome(false, true) == OUTCOME_THROTTLED;
  assert event_intake_outcome(true, false) == OUTCOME_SINK_FAILED;
  assert event_intake_outcome(true, true) == OUTCOME_ACCEPTED;
}

test only_the_accepted_numeral_is_declared_here {
  assert outcome_http_status(OUTCOME_ACCEPTED) == HTTP_ACCEPTED;
  assert outcome_http_status(OUTCOME_MALFORMED) == HTTP_STATUS_OWNED_ELSEWHERE;
  assert outcome_http_status(OUTCOME_THROTTLED) == HTTP_STATUS_OWNED_ELSEWHERE;
  assert outcome_http_status(OUTCOME_SINK_FAILED) == HTTP_STATUS_OWNED_ELSEWHERE;
  assert outcome_http_status(OUTCOME_UNSET) == HTTP_STATUS_OWNED_ELSEWHERE;
  assert MALFORMED_NUMERAL_ALREADY_DECLARED_AT == REUSES_CATALOG_API_ID;
  assert THROTTLED_NUMERAL_ALREADY_DECLARED_AT == REUSES_REQUEST_IDENTITY_ID;
  assert SINK_FAILED_NUMERAL_ALREADY_DECLARED_AT == REUSES_CATALOG_API_ID;
  assert HTTP_ACCEPTED == 202;
  assert CORPUS_FILES_AT_REMEASUREMENT == 43;
  assert SIBLINGS_DECLARING_THIS_NUMERAL == 0;
}

test the_outcome_set_is_closed {
  assert outcome_is_known(OUTCOME_ACCEPTED) == true;
  assert outcome_is_known(OUTCOME_SINK_FAILED) == true;
  assert outcome_is_known(OUTCOME_UNSET) == false;
  assert outcome_is_known(OUTCOME_COUNT) == false;
  assert outcome_is_known(99) == false;
}

test truncation_bounds_the_row_and_leaves_short_values_alone {
  assert sanitized_length(0, SERVER_MESSAGE_CAP_CHARS) == 0;
  assert sanitized_length(500, SERVER_MESSAGE_CAP_CHARS) == 500;
  assert sanitized_length(SERVER_MESSAGE_CAP_CHARS, SERVER_MESSAGE_CAP_CHARS) == SERVER_MESSAGE_CAP_CHARS;
  assert sanitized_length(9000, SERVER_MESSAGE_CAP_CHARS) == SERVER_MESSAGE_CAP_CHARS;
  assert sanitized_length(9000, SERVER_STACK_CAP_CHARS) == SERVER_STACK_CAP_CHARS;
}

test the_two_ends_disagree_about_the_stack_and_agree_about_the_message {
  assert MESSAGE_CAPS_AGREE == true;
  assert BROWSER_MESSAGE_CAP_CHARS == SERVER_MESSAGE_CAP_CHARS;
  assert STACK_CAPS_AGREE == false;
  assert BROWSER_STACK_CAP_CHARS > SERVER_STACK_CAP_CHARS;
  assert stack_survives_the_round_trip(0) == true;
  assert stack_survives_the_round_trip(SERVER_STACK_CAP_CHARS) == true;
  assert stack_survives_the_round_trip(BROWSER_STACK_CAP_CHARS) == false;
}

test a_report_is_attributable_only_because_a_client_said_so {
  assert ID_IS_DERIVED_FROM_HEADERS == false;
  assert SHIPPED_SENDER_SUPPLIES_AN_ID == false;
  assert stored_report_is_attributable(true) == true;
  assert stored_report_is_attributable(false) == false;
}

test one_accepted_event_name_is_stored_and_counted_by_nothing {
  assert EVENT_NAMES_ACCEPTED - EVENT_NAMES_WITH_A_METRIC == EVENT_NAMES_STORED_BUT_UNCOUNTED;
  assert stored_event_name_is_the_clients(true) == true;
  assert stored_event_name_is_the_clients(false) == false;
  assert event_reaches_a_metric(true, true) == true;
  assert event_reaches_a_metric(true, false) == false;
  assert event_reaches_a_metric(false, true) == false;
}

test no_retention_is_claimed_because_none_is_implemented {
  assert TELEMETRY_RETENTION_IS_IMPLEMENTED == false;
  assert AUDIT_SWEEP_MECHANISM_EXISTS == true;
  assert TABLES_ENROLLED_IN_THE_SWEEP == 3;
  assert TELEMETRY_TABLES_ENROLLED_IN_THE_SWEEP == 0;
}

test the_opaque_refusal_needs_every_absence_at_once {
  assert report_is_opaque(true, true, true, true) == true;
  assert report_is_opaque(false, true, true, true) == false;
  assert report_is_opaque(true, false, true, true) == false;
  assert report_is_opaque(true, true, false, true) == false;
  assert report_is_opaque(true, true, true, false) == false;
}

test the_listener_rule_is_two_independent_refusals {
  assert listener_report_is_reportable(true, false, false, false, false) == false;
  assert listener_report_is_reportable(true, true, true, true, true) == false;
  assert listener_report_is_reportable(false, true, true, true, true) == false;
  assert listener_report_is_reportable(false, true, false, true, true) == true;
  assert listener_report_is_reportable(false, true, true, false, true) == true;
  assert listener_report_is_reportable(false, true, true, true, false) == true;
  assert listener_report_is_reportable(false, false, true, true, true) == true;
}

test the_three_paths_are_filtered_differently {
  assert path_is_known(PATH_UNSET) == false;
  assert path_is_known(PATH_LISTENER) == true;
  assert path_is_known(PATH_PANIC) == true;
  assert path_is_known(4) == false;
  assert path_applies_the_opaque_filter(PATH_LISTENER) == true;
  assert path_applies_the_opaque_filter(PATH_REJECTION) == false;
  assert path_applies_the_opaque_filter(PATH_PANIC) == false;
  assert path_applies_the_noise_filter(PATH_LISTENER) == true;
  assert path_applies_the_noise_filter(PATH_REJECTION) == true;
  assert path_applies_the_noise_filter(PATH_PANIC) == false;
}

test every_path_reaches_the_sink_and_the_panic_path_reaches_nothing_else {
  assert path_reaches_the_sink(PATH_LISTENER) == true;
  assert path_reaches_the_sink(PATH_REJECTION) == true;
  assert path_reaches_the_sink(PATH_PANIC) == true;
  assert path_reaches_the_panel(PATH_LISTENER) == true;
  assert path_reaches_the_panel(PATH_REJECTION) == true;
  assert path_reaches_the_panel(PATH_PANIC) == false;
  assert path_records_without_showing(PATH_PANIC) == true;
  assert path_records_without_showing(PATH_LISTENER) == false;
}

test hiding_a_report_from_the_customer_also_hides_it_from_the_shop {
  assert filtering_costs_the_record(PATH_LISTENER) == true;
  assert filtering_costs_the_record(PATH_REJECTION) == true;
  assert filtering_costs_the_record(PATH_PANIC) == false;
}

test the_panel_geometry_is_real_and_its_default_state_is_not_the_panel {
  assert SURVEY_GEOMETRY_CLAIM_IS_CORRECT == true;
  assert PANEL_IS_FIXED == true;
  assert PANEL_MAX_HEIGHT_VH == 50;
  assert PANEL_Z_INDEX == 99999;
  assert SURVEY_CALLED_THE_PANEL_THE_DEFAULT_STATE == true;
  assert PANEL_IS_EXPANDED_BY_DEFAULT == false;
  assert PANEL_OPENS_ONLY_ON_A_CUSTOMER_TAP == true;
}

test nothing_covers_the_shop_until_a_customer_asks_it_to {
  assert anything_renders(false) == false;
  assert anything_renders(true) == true;
  assert panel_blocks_the_screen(false, false) == false;
  assert panel_blocks_the_screen(false, true) == false;
  assert panel_blocks_the_screen(true, false) == false;
  assert panel_blocks_the_screen(true, true) == true;
}

test the_fatal_alert_branch_cannot_fire_on_a_normalized_source {
  assert SOURCE_IS_NORMALIZED_BEFORE_THE_ALERT_TEST == true;
  assert alert_fatal_branch_can_fire(true) == false;
  assert alert_fatal_branch_can_fire(false) == true;
  assert ALERT_TRIGGER_COUNT == 2;
  assert ALERT_TRIGGERS_REACHABLE_IN_PRODUCTION == 1;
}

test a_panic_off_the_purchase_path_pages_nobody {
  assert alert_is_raised(true, true, false, false) == false;
  assert alert_is_raised(true, true, true, false) == true;
  assert alert_is_raised(true, false, true, false) == true;
  assert alert_is_raised(false, true, false, false) == true;
  assert alert_is_raised(true, true, true, true) == false;
  assert alert_is_raised(false, true, false, true) == false;
}

test the_two_mappers_agree_on_seven_arms_and_diverge_on_the_eighth {
  assert surface_is_known(SURFACE_API) == true;
  assert surface_is_known(SURFACE_CHECKOUT) == true;
  assert surface_is_known(SURFACE_UNSET) == false;
  assert API_MAPPED_ARM_COUNT - CHECKOUT_MAPPED_ARM_COUNT == 1;
  assert EXTRA_ARM_IS_THE_EXPIRED_SESSION == true;
  assert CHECKOUT_MAPPER_IS_A_WRAPPER_OF_THE_API_MAPPER == false;
}

test a_failure_renders_a_sentence_a_key_or_a_code_and_never_nothing {
  assert render_kind(SURFACE_API, true, true) == RENDER_LOCALIZED;
  assert render_kind(SURFACE_API, false, true) == RENDER_LOCALIZED;
  assert render_kind(SURFACE_API, true, false) == RENDER_BARE_KEY;
  assert render_kind(SURFACE_API, false, false) == RENDER_BARE_KEY;
  assert render_kind(SURFACE_CHECKOUT, true, true) == RENDER_LOCALIZED;
  assert render_kind(SURFACE_CHECKOUT, true, false) == RENDER_BARE_KEY;
  assert render_kind(SURFACE_CHECKOUT, false, true) == RENDER_BARE_CODE;
  assert render_kind(SURFACE_CHECKOUT, false, false) == RENDER_BARE_CODE;
  assert RENDER_EMPTY_STRING_IS_POSSIBLE == false;
}

test the_bare_code_lives_on_exactly_one_surface {
  assert renders_a_bare_code(SURFACE_CHECKOUT, false) == true;
  assert renders_a_bare_code(SURFACE_CHECKOUT, true) == false;
  assert renders_a_bare_code(SURFACE_API, false) == false;
  assert renders_a_bare_code(SURFACE_API, true) == false;
  assert render_kind_is_known(RENDER_UNSET) == false;
  assert render_kind_is_known(RENDER_LOCALIZED) == true;
  assert render_kind_is_known(RENDER_BARE_CODE) == true;
}

test a_body_code_outranks_the_status_and_an_unknown_one_costs_nothing {
  assert checkout_message_source(true, true) == MESSAGE_FROM_BODY_CODE;
  assert checkout_message_source(true, false) == MESSAGE_FROM_BODY_CODE;
  assert checkout_message_source(false, true) == MESSAGE_FROM_STATUS;
  assert checkout_message_source(false, false) == MESSAGE_FROM_BARE_CODE;
  assert MAPPED_BODY_CODE_COUNT == 1;
  assert MAPPED_BODY_CODE_COUNT_BEFORE_2026_09_25 == MAPPED_BODY_CODE_COUNT + 1;
  assert UNKNOWN_BODY_CODE_IS_EVER_RENDERED == false;
}

test the_seven_ownership_edges_are_named_and_distinct {
